# Short Report (100--150 words)

A common example of poor digital communication is when a student posts a
sarcastic or angry comment about a college teacher or class group on
social media. For instance, a student might complain publicly about a
professor after receiving low marks. The post could be shared widely
among classmates, eventually reaching the professor or college
administration. This situation may lead to misunderstandings,
disciplinary action, or damage to the student's reputation.

This problem could have been avoided by using responsible digital
communication. Instead of posting publicly, the student could have
discussed the issue politely with the teacher through email or in
person. Thinking before posting, maintaining respectful language, and
using private communication channels are better ways to handle
disagreements online.
